      "id": "adv_math.C8.S01.P026",
      "subject": "高等数学",
      "chapter": "第8章",
      "section": "概览",
      "label": "8.5",
      "title": ".2 方程组的情形",
      "details": "下面将隐函数存在定理作另一方面的推广，不仅增加方程中变量的个数，而且增加方程的个数。例如，考虑方程组\n\n$$\n\\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l} F (x, y, z) = 0, \\\\ G (x, y, z) = 0. \\end{array} \\right.\n$$\n\n这三个变量只有一个变量独立变化, 可以确定两个一元函数\n\n定理8.5.3 设三元函数  $F(x,y,x), G(x,y,z)$  在点  $P_{0}(x_{0},y_{0},z_{0})$  的某个邻域内有一阶连续偏导数, 又  $F(x_{0},y_{0},z_{0}) = 0, G(x_{0},y_{0},z_{0}) = 0$  且偏导数组成的函数行列式 (或称雅可比 (Jacobi) 行列式)\n\n$$\nJ = \\frac {\\partial (F , G)}{\\partial (y , z)} = \\left| \\begin{array}{c c} F _ {y} & F _ {z} \\\\ G _ {y} & G _ {z} \\end{array} \\right|\n$$\n\n在点  $P_0$  处不为零, 则方程组  $\\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l} F(x,y,z) = 0, \\\\ G(x,y,z) = 0 \\end{array} \\right.$  在  $P_0$  的某一邻域内唯一确定一组单值有连续一阶导数的函数  $y = f(x)$  及  $z = g(x)$ , 满足  $f(x_0) = y_0$ ,  $g(x_0) = z_0$ ,  $F(x,f(x);g(x)) \\equiv 0$ ,  $G(x,f(x),g(x)) \\equiv 0$ , 并且有\n\n$$\n\\frac {\\mathrm {d} y}{\\mathrm {d} x} = - \\frac {1}{J} \\frac {\\partial (F , G)}{\\partial (x , z)}, \\quad \\frac {\\mathrm {d} z}{\\mathrm {d} x} = - \\frac {1}{J} \\frac {\\partial (F , G)}{\\partial (y , x)}.\n$$\n\n通常将  $\\left| \\begin{array}{ll}f_u & f_v\\\\ g_u & g_v \\end{array} \\right| = f_ug_v - f_vg_u$  记作  $\\frac{\\partial(f,g)}{\\partial(u,v)}$  ，上面就使用了这种记号.\n\n同样, 这里不对定理加以证明, 只推导求导公式. 对方程组\n\n$$\n\\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l l} F (x, f (x), g (x)) \\equiv 0, \\\\ G (x, f (x), g (x)) \\equiv 0 \\end{array} \\right.\n$$\n\n中两个方程两边分别对  $x$  求导，得到\n\n$$\n\\left\\{ \\begin{array}{l} F _ {x} + F _ {y} \\frac {\\mathrm {d} y}{\\mathrm {d} x} + F _ {z} \\frac {\\mathrm {d} z}{\\mathrm {d} x} = 0, \\\\ G _ {x} + G _ {y} \\frac {\\mathrm {d} y}{\\mathrm {d} x} + G _ {z} \\frac {\\mathrm {d} z}{\\mathrm {d} x} = 0, \\end{array} \\right.\n$$\n\n用消元法解得\n\n$$\n\\frac {\\mathrm {d} y}{\\mathrm {d} x} = \\frac {- F _ {x} G _ {z} + F _ {z} G _ {x}}{F _ {y} G _ {z} - F _ {z} G _ {y}} = - \\frac {\\left| \\begin{array}{l l} F _ {x} & F _ {z} \\\\ G _ {x} & G _ {z} \\end{array} \\right|}{\\left| \\begin{array}{l l} F _ {y} & F _ {z} \\\\ G _ {y} & G _ {z} \\end{array} \\right|} = - \\frac {1}{J} \\frac {\\partial (F , G)}{\\partial (x , z)}.\n$$\n\n同理可得\n\n$$\n\\frac {\\mathrm {d} z}{\\mathrm {d} x} = - \\frac {1}{J} \\frac {...",
